# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info
# OS metadata
.DS_Store

# LaTeX build artifacts (paper/ispa2026/main.pdf is covered by *.pdf below)
paper/ispa2026/*.aux
paper/ispa2026/*.log
paper/ispa2026/*.out

# Virtual environments
.venv

# Office lock files ("~$report.docx" appears while Word has the file open)
~$*

# Experiment outputs
#
# Regenerable artifacts stay out of version control. The exceptions are the
# result sets behind docs/pilot_v2_report.md: outputs/claude_v2/ is the first
# delivery, outputs/claude_v2_reviewfix/ is the first review round, and
# outputs/claude_v2_reviewfix2/ is the second and the one the report now cites.
# Their run records, replay tables and diagnostic figures are kept so the
# reported numbers can be checked without re-running anything, and so each
# correction can be compared against what it replaced. Everything else under
# outputs/ is rebuilt by the commands in scripts/README.md.
#
# outputs/mechanism_probe_audit/ is the evidence set behind
# docs/mechanism_applicability_report.md. It holds only slim projected tables
# plus a provenance manifest; the wide per-cell CSVs it is projected from stay
# untracked under outputs/mechanism_probe/.
#
# outputs/ht_natural_corridor_audit/ is the evidence set behind
# docs/ht_natural_corridor_report.md -- the WEN38 natural-corridor diagnostic.
#
# outputs/handoff_20260925/ is the evidence set behind
# docs/model_value_pilot_report.md and docs/research_readiness_report.md -- the
# 2026-09-25 local handoff reproduction. Unlike the sets above it keeps the full
# run records, executions and instance snapshots, because the reports cite 1475
# replay rows and 58 searches that have to be re-checkable in place.
#
# outputs/report_reproduction/ is the delivery root behind docs/wen38_*.md and
# the Word report. Only two slim sets are versioned, plus the small provenance
# files the report cites: analysis/ (the projected quality, pairing and
# representative tables -- the same shape as mechanism_probe_audit/),
# ec_diagnosis/, commands.sh, protocol.json and input_roots.json. The 267M
# report/ build, the budget_*/ and corridor/ run records, the publication
# figures and the Word delivery zip stay local; commands.sh rebuilds them.
#
# Note the wildcard: "outputs/" would exclude the directory itself, and a
# file inside an excluded directory cannot be re-included.
outputs/*
!outputs/claude_v2/
!outputs/claude_v2_reviewfix/
!outputs/claude_v2_reviewfix2/
!outputs/mechanism_probe_audit/
!outputs/ht_natural_corridor_audit/
!outputs/handoff_20260925/
!outputs/report_reproduction/
outputs/report_reproduction/*
!outputs/report_reproduction/analysis/
!outputs/report_reproduction/ec_diagnosis/
!outputs/report_reproduction/commands.sh
!outputs/report_reproduction/protocol.json
!outputs/report_reproduction/input_roots.json
figures/
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.svg
*.pdf
!references/*.pdf
# The paper PDF is versioned so the current build can be previewed without a
# TeX toolchain. It is a build artifact: re-run pdflatex (twice, for the
# bibliography) after editing main.tex, or it will be stale.
!paper/ispa2026/main.pdf

# Must come after the extension rules above, which would otherwise exclude
# the diagnostic figures. The handoff report figures need their directory
# re-included as well, since "figures/" matches it.
!outputs/claude_v2/pilot_diagnostics.png
!outputs/claude_v2_reviewfix/pilot_diagnostics.png
!outputs/claude_v2_reviewfix2/pilot_diagnostics.png
!outputs/handoff_20260925/pilot/figures/
!outputs/handoff_20260925/pilot/figures/*.pdf
!outputs/handoff_20260925/pilot/figures/*.png

# Claude Code worktrees are per-session working directories, not repo content
.claude/worktrees/
